   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 20 of the laws of 2015, appropriating money for\ncertain municipal corporations and school districts, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7057",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7057-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part C Subpart H §4, Chap 20 of 2015",
    "lawSection": "Municipalities",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7057\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 20 of the laws of 2015, appropriating money for\ncertain municipal corporations and school districts, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThe specific objective of the proposed legislation is to remove the\nsunset provision from the statute that authorizes the Electric Generat-\ning Facility Cessation Mitigation Program (the \"Program\"). The Program\nis currently set to expire on July 1, 2025.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThe bill amends section 4 of subpart H of Part C of chapter 20 of the\nlaws of 2015 by removing the sunset provision of the Electric Generating\nFacility Cessation Mitigation Fund, thereby making the Fund permanent.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Program will be increasingly needed in future years. The recently\nenacted Climate Leadership and Community Protection Act mandates a\ndramatic decrease in the State's greenhouse gas emissions and meeting\nthis goal will require the elimination of fossil fuel electric generat-\ning facilities. Many of these facilities contribute significantly to the\nlocal tax base and local economy. By mitigating the tax losses caused by\nthese closures, the Program plays a vital role in maintaining local\nservices such as fire, police and particularly the schools. Knowing that\nthe Program will continue to be in place will help alleviate local\nanxiety about these closures and thereby assist the State in meeting its\nemissions reduction goals. This is now a pressing issue because the\nProgram sunset is only five years away and if left in place would\nprevent any current or future Program participants from receiving the\nfull seven years of assistance intended by the fund.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately.\n",
